Z||000000||wxxo||03-29-2000||01:15 PM||||does anyone know anything about headlight motors??? i got a new pair, put them in the car, flipped the switch and nothing!!! they will go down but will not come up?? cant figure this one out. there is a lot of resistance when i try to crank them up manually. what does that sound like to yall?? the lights work but thats it. im stuck on this one. any help is greatly appreciated. thanks ||||reg||5
Z||000001||batboy||03-29-2000||01:37 PM||||The earlier model headlights are different than the later models. You need to tell us what year your Fiero is.||||reg||1
Z||000002||wxxo||03-29-2000||02:16 PM||||duhh... haha its an 86.. sorry. i know 84 -86 had crappy motors but im sure that these motors work. it must be something in the wiring. anyhow thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DRH||03-29-2000||03:42 PM||||Check the link below for a ton of info about the Fiero headlight system.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.tir.com/~jaski/headlight.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tir.com/~jaski/headlight.htm</A> ||||reg||3
Z||000004||AL||03-30-2000||09:33 PM||||waxxo check the 2 red wires near  the master cylinder,both of those wires have to be connected to one wire, if they are go to your relays, pull one at a time, once you have one out don't disconnect them, turn your switch for the lights and then try to sqeeze it from side to side you should here clicking noises coming from the relay, do that to all of them and if they all click then it's the relay by the headlight, the one in front, drivers side, change that one out and it shoud work, good luck,AL. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||wxxo||03-31-2000||05:37 PM||||thanks for all of the replies. i figured out what the problem was. faulty switch in the passenger comp. (the one that  operates the headlights) that thing has been giving me problems for some time. inside there are three little metal fingers. (the middle one was flipping me the bird haha) anyhow there is one for the parking lights, one for the headlights and one for the headlight motors. the only reason that i mention it now is because i looked all over the place for things that could be wrong and none of them said to check that switch. just thought that id pass that bit of info along so that if anyone else is having similar problems they might want to check the switch. i should have known in the first place because the damn thing actually caught on fire one time when i was foolin with it. i guess that the 86 se's caught on fire too hahaha. thanks again everyone.||||reg||1
